> A hand-checkable calculation

One zero-mean unit-variance Gaussian gives NLL.5*log(2*pi) at target0. The full model uses three diagonal-Gaussian components in eight latent dimensions. The controller is evolved against real pixel CartPole; the source dreams only at the end.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/world_models_worked.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -lpthread -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){std::filesystem::create_directories("build");auto nll=dm::nn::models::WorldMdnNll(dm::nn::zeros({1,3}),dm::nn::zeros({1,1}),1,1);std::vector<double>values{nll.item<double>(),.5*std::log(2*3.14159265f)};std::print("| coordinate | computed value |\n|---:|---:|\n");for(size_t i=0;i<values.size();++i)std::print("| {} | {:.9f} |\n",i,values[i]);std::vector<double>x(values.size());std::iota(x.begin(),x.end(),0.);double low=std::min(0.,*std::min_element(values.begin(),values.end())),high=std::max(0.,*std::max_element(values.begin(),values.end())),span=std::max(1.,high-low);dm::graphics::RPlot::create().bars(x,values,"computed values",{37,99,235}).ylim(low-.05*span,high+.05*span).title("world models worked calculation").size(1000,550).save_svg("build/world_models_worked.svg");}
