> Actual source performance

These measurements come from the complete source run above; each series retains source execution order. A bounded run or one evaluation point does not establish convergence. Model loss and task return use separate figures.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/world_models_diagnostic0.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -lpthread -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){auto archive=dm::nn::load_npz("build/world_models_source.npz");auto plot=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();int series=0;for(const auto&[key,t]:archive){if(!key.starts_with("vae_nll"))continue;auto y=t.to_vector<double>();std::vector<double>x(y.size());std::iota(x.begin(),x.end(),0.);plot.lines(x,y,key,{37+(series%4)*50,99,235-(series%4)*50}).points(x,y,key+" points",{37+(series%4)*50,99,235-(series%4)*50},3);++series;}if(!series)throw std::runtime_error("source diagnostic missing");plot.title("world models actual source diagnostics").x_label("VAE update").y_label("Nats per frame").size(1100,600).save_svg("build/world_models_diagnostic0.svg");}
